> **Self-exclusion (phantom / nickname-conflation identity):** no Anthropic product named "Claude Opus 3.7" has ever been released. The name resolves to (a) a **user-community codename for the throttled/limited Opus 4.6** and (b) a **citation/conflation artifact** with Claude 3.7 Sonnet. Every capability benchmark row below reads "no verified public score found". This file is saved as `.excluded` so `pnpm sync` skips it; no scores below are used in averages.

## Model card (identity resolution)

- **Name:** Claude Opus 3.7 (`claude-opus-3.7`) — **does not exist as a released model.** Anthropic's Opus lineage runs 4 → 4.1 → **4.4 → 4.5 → 4.6 → 4.7 → 5 → 5.5**; its early-2025 "3.7" release was **Claude 3.7 Sonnet** (Feb 2025, hybrid reasoning) — never an Opus 3.7. No `claude-opus-3-7` API id appears on llm-stats, llm-registry, BenchLM, OpenRouter, or any provider catalog (searched 2026-10-27).
- **What the name actually is — three documented noise sources:**
  1. **Community codename for the "limited opus" (Apr 2026).** Verbatim from comment #7 by user `rurban` on the official `anthropics/claude-code` issue [#42796](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/42796) (Apr 6, 2026, 👍15): *"Indeed, codex with gpt-5.4 bypassed opus-4.6 since about February in complex tasks. It's also cheaper and faster. **We gave the limited opus the codename opus—3.7**."* "We" = the commenter's team; the "limited opus" is Opus 4.6 served at reduced thinking/effort (the issue documents the Feb–Mar 2026 redaction/medium-effort rollout). The codename is a *mocking downgrade label* ("it now behaves like a hypothetical 3.7"), not a product.
  2. **Erroneous academic citation predating the nickname.** Ravenea (arXiv 2505.14462, May 2025; ICLR 2026 proceedings) cites *"Claude Opus 3.7 (Anthropic, 2024)"* — wrong year and wrong product line in the same phrase; a generation-era citation hallucination.
  3. **Speculation / SEO / reseller adopters of the slang.** Medium's Optimus Alpha deep-dive hedges *"perhaps Opus 3.7?"*; a content-farm pingback advertises "GPT 5.5 vs Claude Opus 3.7: Pricing & Comparison 2026"; a Threads reseller lists "8折claude opus 3.7"; a hand-maintained portfolio config (miasma, PRICING_LAST_UPDATED 2026-09-16) carries a `'claude-opus-3-7': 0.51` / `'opus-3-7': (6.0, 25.2)` entry matching no Anthropic rate card.
- **Ambiguous references noted, not counted:** Roboflow X ("we ran [Claude Opus 3.7] through our eval" vs GPT-5.5) gives no model id or numbers — consistent with either the slang or a 3.7-Sonnet misname; HN/LinkedIn/biorxiv/YouTube usage mentions (incl. "Kimi k2.6 Nears Claude Opus 3.7") all postdate or echo the nickname era. None is a first-party release record.
- **Provider / access:** none — no Model Studio/API id, no OpenRouter id, no system card, no pricing page, no Anthropic news post ever found.
- **Release / knowledge:** n/a — never released. (A real "Opus 3.7" would predate Opus 4.0/May 2025, yet every reference is 2025-2026 conflation or nickname-era — the timeline is incoherent for a product.)
- **IDs:** none found (`claude-opus-3-7` never observed in any catalog).
- **Context window:** n/a. **Modalities:** n/a. **Pricing:** n/a (the lone `opus-3-7: (6.0, 25.2)` config row matches no official card). **Architecture:** n/a.

