### Research trail (why this is excluded)

1. Six web searches on 2026-10-27 — `"Claude Opus 3.7" Anthropic model release`; `"Claude Opus 3.7" release date benchmarks SWE-bench pricing 2025`; `"Optimus Alpha" OpenRouter Anthropic "Opus 3.7" stealth model identified`; `"claude-opus-3-7" OR "claude opus 3.7" benchlm OR llm-stats OR openrouter model page price`; `"opus-3-7" OR "claude-opus-3.7" API models list OR pricing per million tokens Anthropic`; exact-phrase `"We gave the limited opus the codename"` — plus two fetches (issue #42796 and its timeline) confirming the rurban comment verbatim.
2. The catalog sweep is decisive: no llm-stats / llm-registry / BenchLM / OpenRouter / provider page exists for the name, while every retrievable mention is one of the three noise sources above. No launch post, no pricing page, no system card, no benchmark table anywhere.
3. Per contract: zero verified public benchmark numbers → `.md.excluded`, never invented numbers. The `average.md` present in this folder could not have come from a real `claude-opus-3-7` evaluation and should be reviewed by the project owner — the intended identity is most likely **Claude 3.7 Sonnet** (a real Feb-2025 model), which would need its own slug; a secondary possibility is that the folder tracks the Opus-4.6 "limited" nickname, which is not a model.
4. Note: this folder is not in `model-queue.md` (despite containing an `average.md`), so no scores are pending in the current roster.

